  {
   "id": "parallel-12bit",
   "title": "Parallel cascading, comparing 12-bit words",
   "page": 12,
   "description": "Four comparators in two ranks compare two 12-bit words. Three first-rank comparators work on slices of the words at the same time; the upper two use their cascade inputs IA<B and IA>B as one more bit pair, and the lowest has IA<B and IA>B LOW, IA=B HIGH, and its A0, B0, A1 and B1 tied to GND. Their A<B and A>B outputs go to a fourth comparator as bit pairs: the top slice as the B3/A3 pair, the middle slice as B2/A2, while the lowest slice drives the fourth comparator's cascade inputs. Its unused bit inputs A0, B0, A1 and B1 are tied to GND. The fourth comparator gives the final A<B, A=B and A>B outputs. The A=B outputs of the two upper first-rank comparators are left open.",
